.TH MDT.ENABLE_PARALLEL_RENAME_CROSSDIR 4 2026-10-06 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir \- parallel cross-directory rename of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir= ENABLE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 | -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present for MDT devices.
.TP
.B Default
.RB enable_parallel_rename_crossdir= 1
.SH DESCRIPTION
The boolean
.B enable_parallel_rename_crossdir
parameter controls whether renaming a non-directory from one directory
to another may proceed without the filesystem-wide rename lock.
If
.I ENABLE
is
.B 1
(or aliases
.BR on " or " true ),
these renames are permitted to run in parallel. If it is
.B 0
or
.B off
they take the rename lock.
.PP
Within a striped directory the parent of a name is the stripe that
holds it, so a rename between names on different stripes is a
cross-directory rename.
.PP
This parameter applies only when
.B enable_parallel_rename_file
is enabled. A rename whose source parent or source object is on another
MDT is also governed by
.BR enable_parallel_rename_remote .
A directory renamed between two directories always takes the rename
lock, since it can change the directory hierarchy.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following module:
.EX
.B mdt.*.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Disable parallel cross-directory rename of files on the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-*.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir=0"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B enable_parallel_rename_crossdir
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.16.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_15_60-28-ge66dd92775
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_dir (4),
